    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "definition",
     "title": "Data and information",
     "md": "**Data** is raw facts and figures with no meaning on their own, e.g. 15, 12, 18. **Information** is data that has been processed and organised so that it has meaning, e.g. 'The class average mark is 15'."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "retenir",
     "title": "Processing cycle",
     "md": "The cycle has stages: **collect** the data, **input** it, **process** it (sort, calculate, search), **output** the information, **store** it. Information can then be used to make decisions."
    },
