    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "definition",
     "title": "Database",
     "md": "A **database** is an organised collection of data that can be searched and updated easily. It is stored in **tables**. A table has **fields** (columns, e.g. Name) and **records** (rows, e.g. all data about one student). A **primary key** is a field with a unique value for each record, such as StudentID."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "retenir",
     "title": "Data types",
     "md": "Each field has a **data type**: **text** (names, phone numbers), **number** (age, price), **date** (birthday), **yes/no** (a true/false answer). Choosing the right type helps sorting and validation. A phone number is stored as text because we do not calculate with it."
    },
