   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "definition",
     "title": "Network",
     "md": "A **network** is two or more computers connected so that they can share **data**, **printers** and an **Internet connection**. Computers in a network are linked by cables or by wireless (**Wi-Fi**)."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "retenir",
     "title": "LAN and WAN",
     "md": "A **LAN** (local area network) covers a small area such as a school or an office. A **WAN** (wide area network) covers a large area; the **Internet** is the largest WAN. Reasons for networking: sharing resources, saving money, central storage and backup, communication."
    },
