    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "retenir",
     "title": "Topologies and devices",
     "md": "**Star**: each computer connects to a central **switch**. **Bus**: all computers share one cable. A **router** connects a network to the Internet. A **network interface card (NIC)** lets a computer join a network. A **server** is a computer that provides services to others."
    },
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "pieges",
     "title": "Mistakes",
     "md": "- A network is not the same as the Internet.\n- In a star network, if the central switch fails, all connected computers lose the network.\n- Wireless networks are convenient but can be less secure if not protected with a password."
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 1",
     "statement": "A school lab in Garoua has 15 computers and one printer. Why connect them in a LAN?",
     "steps": [
      "All 15 computers can print on the one printer.",
      "Files can be shared and one Internet connection can serve all."
     ],
     "answer": "To share the printer, files and Internet connection."
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Example 2",
     "statement": "One cable of a star network is cut. How many computers are affected if there are 10 computers?",
